+// Ported from apps/floor_planner/test/document_replace_test.dart (audit
+// docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-architecture-demo-test-audit.md, section
+// "document_replace_test.dart"): RP1-RP8, RN1-RN3, all PORT. New, Open and
+// Open sample ask Save / Don't Save / Cancel before they replace a dirty
+// plan -- for Open, before the picker -- and replace a clean one without
+// asking. Save runs the Save step inside the flow's busy span: a cancelled
+// or failed save keeps everything, and a save that succeeded while an edit
+// landed asks again. While the nested save is held, nothing else runs.
+//
+// Decided: premise impossible (spec decision 5): the old tests asserted
+// every toolbar button *disabled* while a flow runs. `PlanEditor` has no
+// host hook to grey its buttons, so the app's file callbacks do nothing
+// while busy and the buttons stay enabled. Every "disabled" loop below is
+// therefore its `-open` form: the busy flag is up, the buttons are still
+// built enabled, and a tap or a chord starts no second flow. Undo and Redo
+// are the library's own and are not held either (decision 5 does not toggle
+// `PlanPermissions`): see RN1-open-undo.
+//
+// RP7 drives the flows through the toolbar buttons, not by calling them: the
+// editor settles pending input before it calls the host's callback
+// (`PlanController.settlePendingInput` is internal to the library, so the
+// host cannot), which is the path of every button and chord of the app.
